-- The cast block (w1): Noita's draw algorithm is a scan. Twin of 120-cast-block.bqn (main wand). (was w1-cast-block)
-- The wand-construction stress test begins here. Each card adds or spends draw; the cast block ends where the running balance first touches zero — the draw algorithm, discovered to be a scan.
-- Wand [Double, SB, SB, SB, DP, SB]. Each card carries drawAdd (multicast 2/3, modifier 1, projectile 0); the block's running balance is 1 + the scan of (drawAdd - 1) along slot order, and the block ends where the balance first touches zero.
-- Membership needs the running MINIMUM, not the balance itself (the -b twin is the trap); min-scan is the negated max-scan; the membership gather reads prev over the deck view — slot 0 enters by fiat, everything after enters iff every earlier balance stayed positive.
--! registry ../registries/120-cast-block.reg
--! expect bal = 0 2 1 0 -1 -1 -2
--! expect minBal = 0 2 1 0 -1 -1 -2
--! expect member = 0 1 1 1 0 0 0

Spell , Bal = 1 + (+\ (DrawAdd - 1) @ Spell)
Spell , MinBal = 0 - (max\ (0 - Bal) @ Spell)
Spell @ deck & (Slot == 0 | prev.MinBal > 0) , +Member
